from pathlib import Path
import hashlib,json
r=Path('research/frontier-44-special-representation-examples-28-six-step-owner-escalation-repairs/cyclotomic_isomorphism')
h=json.loads((r/'current-hashes.json').read_text())
def edit(n,fn):
 p=Path('items')/(n+'.md');assert hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest()==h[str(p)];p.write_text(fn(p.read_text()));h[str(p)]=hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest();(r/'current-hashes.json').write_text(json.dumps(h,indent=2)+'\n')
def reverse(s):
 a=s.index('[F1]');b=s.index('[F2]',a)
 s=s[:a]+r'''[F1] The explicit five-branch scalar series and their pair-product/interchange identities are those proved in steps 1.2–1.3 of [[lem-cyclotomic-hecke-intertwiners-and-local-power-series]]. Only these scalar identities, not Hecke-side intertwiner relations, are used before establishing the Hecke presentation.

'''+s[b:]
 a=s.index('1.1 The homogeneous');b=s.index('2.1 The cyclotomic',a)
 s=s[:a]+r'''1.1 A faithful KLR calculation, before quotient. Use independent dots and the rational operators of the normalization supplier's steps 3.1–3.2: equal crossings act by $D=(S-1)/(u-v)$ and unequal crossings by $Sc_{ij}$, where $c_{ij}=(1-p)/N_{ij}$ in DG or $(1-P)/N_{ij}$ in NG. The pair product is exactly $K_{ij}$ and the five braid computations give corrections $0,1,-1,u+w-2v$, with the specified braid order. Thus these operators satisfy the affine sign-modified KLR presentation. This representation is faithful for formal dot coefficients: moving dots right by the proved sliding rule, use quadratic relations to remove repeated simple reflections and braid relations to reduce each crossing word to a chosen reduced word plus shorter words. This terminates by length (and the finite Coxeter reduction at each fixed length), giving a spanning family $\psi_we(i)$. Its leading permutation coefficient is a product of nonzero $c_{ij}$ and of $1/(u-v)$ for equal pairs; proper subwords have smaller permutation length. Maximal-length comparison in the matrix crossed product therefore proves independence of the formal coefficients. Clearing finitely many temporary dot differences is legitimate in this faithful affine calculation. It does not assert faithfulness after taking the cyclotomic quotient. [F1, F2, algebra]

1.2 The mixed and quadratic computations. In the representation of step 1.1, the displayed inverse Hecke element $\psi N-p$ (DG) or $\psi N-P$ (NG) is literally $S(1-\widehat p)-\widehat p$ or $S(1-\widehat P)-\widehat P$ on every word. On unequal colours this follows by cancellation of the right coefficient $N$; on equal colours $\psi=D$ and $D N-1=H$ by the equality $H+1=(S+1)(-N/(u-v))$. The supplier's step 2.2 gives the mixed relation $Hx_{r+1}-x_rH=1$ in DG, and $HX_rH=qX_{r+1}$ in NG, together with $H^2=1$ or $H^2=(q-1)H+q$. Alternatively the DG mixed constant on an unequal word is $(i_r-i_{r+1}+u-v)p=1$, and on an equal word it is $(u-v)+N=1$; in NG the same spectral substitution gives the stated mixed identity. Commuting dots, distant mixed relations and distant crossings follow because the operators involve disjoint pairs. By step 1.1 these are regular affine-KLR identities and hence evaluate in the nilpotent-dot quotient. [F1, F2, step 1.1, algebra]

1.3 All five Hecke braid patterns. For a triple with distinct colours, adjacent repeated colours $(i,i,k)$ or $(i,k,k)$, outer repeated colours $(i,j,i)$, or all equal colours, the inverse elements of step 1.2 have precisely the same rational Hecke operator $H$ on each successive word. Their two braid products therefore have the six coefficients listed in the supplier's step 2.2; this table applies to each of the five patterns because spectral variables, rather than colour constants, are used in its denominators. The required scalar reductions are $b_{AB}+b_{BA}=t$, $a_{AB}a_{BA}=h+tb_{AB}-b_{AB}^2$, and $b_{AB}b_{BC}=b_{AC}(b_{AB}+b_{BC}-t)$, with $(h,t)=(1,0)$ or $(q,q-1)$. In the outer-repeated pattern the KLR braid correction $u+w-2v$ on a double edge was already included in the faithful model of step 1.1, so it is not suppressed by this table. In the equal pattern $D$ accounts for all divided-difference terms. Equality of the six explicit coefficients, followed by faithfulness, proves Hecke braid inside the formal KLR algebra; its regular expressions descend to the cyclotomic quotient. This proves the missing four cases and the all-equal case without assuming any Hecke intertwiner relation in that algebra. [F1, step 1.1, step 1.2, algebra]

'''+s[b:]
 s=s.replace('Steps 1.1 and 2.1','Steps 1.1–1.3 and 2.1').replace('steps 3.1 and 3.1','steps 3.1 and 4.1').replace('show that it kills exactly the off-diagonal corners','show that it kills all other sector corners')
 s=s[:s.index('## Remarks')]+'''## Remarks

The scalar normalization is checked before the KLR-to-Hecke calculation. The rational model is faithful only before quotient; the identities evaluated in the cyclotomic algebra contain no inverted equal-colour dot differences.
'''
 return s
edit('lem-cyclotomic-klr-block-satisfies-the-hecke-relations',reverse)
def forward(s):
 a=s.index('1.2 The quadratic');b=s.index('2.1',a)
 s=s[:a]+r'''1.2 Quadratic and all braid patterns. Work first in the faithful formal affine-Hecke calculation of the normalization supplier, then evaluate its regular identities in the sector. On equal colours the normalized intertwiner is $D=(S-1)/(u-v)$, so $D^2=0$ and $Dv-uD=1=vD-Du$. On unequal colours it is $Sc_{ij}(u,v)$, with $c=(1-p)/N$ in DG or $(1-P)/N$ in NG; its square is $c_{ij}(u,v)c_{ji}(v,u)=K_{ij}(u,v)$, giving respectively $1,v-u,u-v,(v-u)(u-v)$. For the braid, put $W=S_1S_2S_1$ and dots $u,v,w$. Distinct colours give both words $Wc_{ij}(u,v)c_{ik}(u,w)c_{jk}(v,w)$. For $(i,i,k)$ both words are $(W-S_1S_2)c_{ik}(u,w)c_{ik}(v,w)/(v-w)$; for $(i,k,k)$ they are $(W-S_2S_1)c_{ik}(u,v)c_{ik}(u,w)/(u-v)$, with denominators on the left and coefficient products on the right. The products are symmetric in the two equal-colour variables, so their divided differences vanish. For $(i,j,i)$ the longest terms cancel and the identity coefficients differ by $(K_{ij}(w,v)-K_{ij}(u,v))/(u-w)$; direct substitution gives $0,1,-1,u+w-2v$. On all equal colours the common value is $-(1-S_1-S_2+S_1S_2+S_2S_1-W)/((u-v)(u-w)(v-w))$. These are the supplier's explicit local computations, using only affine-Hecke relations and scalar normalizers, not the opposite relation-map lemma. The double-edge correction and its sign remain valid in characteristic two. Clearing temporary differences in the faithful formal calculation gives regular relations; only those relations, and unit coefficients, are evaluated on nilpotent dots. Hence every quadratic and braid relation (1.14)–(1.15) holds in $H^\Lambda_\alpha$. [F1, F2, algebra]

'''+s[b:]
 return s
edit('lem-hecke-intertwiners-produce-local-klr-generators',forward)
def theorem(s):
 s=s.replace(r'\Phi_rQ_r(i)Q_r(i)^{-1}e(i)',r'\Phi_rQ_r(i)^{-1}Q_r(i)e(i)')
 s=s.replace('Hence $\\rho\\sigma$ fixes every presentation generator of $H^\\Lambda_\\alpha$.',r'''For the polynomial generators the computations are $\rho\sigma(x_re_\alpha)=\sum_i((x_r-i_r)+i_r)e(i)=x_re_\alpha$ in DG and $\rho\sigma(X_re_\alpha)=\sum_iq^{i_r}(1-(1-q^{-i_r}X_r))e(i)=X_re_\alpha$ in NG; their inverses are fixed because homomorphisms preserve inverses. Conversely $\sigma\rho(y_re(i))=(\sigma(x_r)-i_r)e(i)=y_re(i)$ in DG and $(1-q^{-i_r}\sigma(X_r))e(i)=y_re(i)$ in NG. Along with the projector identities of [F1], these verify every presentation generator of both algebras, including the correct inverse NG substitution. Hence $\rho\sigma$ fixes every presentation generator of $H^\Lambda_\alpha$.''')
 return s
edit('thm-cyclotomic-hecke-central-sectors-are-isomorphic-to-type-a-cyclotomic-klr-algebras',theorem)
